[2026-02-04T17:13:24.435Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MP1GVkoDHWWv9KaxDHor6q","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"pharmaceutical companies Medicaid drug pricing deals Trump 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"WATCH: Trump announces 9 pharmaceutical companies will lower drug prices | PBS News\",\"url\":\"https://www.pbs.org/newshour/health/watch-live-trump-expected-to-make-announcement-about-lowering-drug-prices\"},{\"title\":\"Trump Announces Pricing Deals With 9 Drugmakers, Expanding Most-Favored-Nation Drug Pricing Strategy | Pharmacy Times\",\"url\":\"https://www.pharmacytimes.com/view/trump-announces-pricing-deals-with-9-drugmakers-expanding-most-favored-nation-drug-pricing-strategy\"},{\"title\":\"Trump announces new drugmaker deals to lower drug costs, boost US investment | Fox Business\",\"url\":\"https://www.foxbusiness.com/politics/trump-secures-agreements-major-drugmakers-lower-medicaid-prescription-costs-americans\"},{\"title\":\"Fact Sheet: President Donald J. Trump Announces Largest Developments to Date in Bringing Most-Favored-Nation Pricing to American Patients – The White House\",\"url\":\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2025/12/fact-sheet-president-donald-j-trump-announces-largest-developments-to-date-in-bringing-most-favored-nation-pricing-to-american-patients/\"},{\"title\":\"Trump struck deals with 16 drug companies. But they're still raising prices this year\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2026/01/16/nx-s1-5678915/trumprx-pharma-drug-price-deals-list-prices\"},{\"title\":\"Pharma Companies Raise List Prices, Including 16 That Had Agreements to Lower Prices with Trump Administration: Report | PharmExec\",\"url\":\"https://www.pharmexec.com/view/companies-raise-list-prices-16-agreements-lower-prices-trump-administration-report\"},{\"title\":\"Drug Pricing in the Era of Trump 2.0 | Medicare Policy Initiative\",\"url\":\"https://medicare.chir.georgetown.edu/drug-pricing-in-the-era-of-trump-2-0/\"},{\"title\":\"J&J Agreement Brings 15 of 17 Pharma Companies Into Trump's Drug-Pricing Effort | AJMC\",\"url\":\"https://www.ajmc.com/view/j-j-agreement-brings-15-of-17-pharma-companies-into-trump-s-drug-pricing-effort\"},{\"title\":\"Nine drugmakers cut deal with Trump administration to slash medication costs\",\"url\":\"https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/nine-drugmakers-cut-deal-trump-administration-slash-medication-costs-rcna250138\"},{\"title\":\"Pharma companies with Trump deals may avoid Medicare price cuts | STAT\",\"url\":\"https://www.statnews.com/2025/12/23/trump-drug-pricing-deals-medicare-most-favored-nation-demos/\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, here's what I found about pharmaceutical companies, Medicaid drug pricing deals, and the Trump administration in 2025-2026:\n\n## Overview of the Drug Pricing Deals\n\nPresident Trump announced agreements with major pharmaceutical companies to lower prescription drug prices for Americans in line with the lowest prices paid by other developed nations (known as the most-favored-nation, or MFN, price).\n\n### Companies Involved\n\nPharmaceutical companies Amgen, Bristol Myers Squibb, Boehringer Ingelheim, Genentech, Gilead Sciences, GSK, Merck, Novartis and Sanofi agreed to rein in Medicaid drug prices to match what they charged in other developed countries.\n\nOther major drugmakers including Pfizer, AstraZeneca, EMD Serono, Novo Nordisk and Eli Lilly struck similar deals with the Trump administration earlier in 2025.\n\nWith Johnson & Johnson's participation, 15 of 17 companies contacted by the administration over the summer have now signed on.\n\n### Key Details of the Deals\n\nThe agreements include direct-to-consumer sales, bypassing insurance, with a federal platform, TrumpRx.gov, launching in 2026. Companies aligning with Most Favored Nation pricing receive a 3-year tariff suspension, avoiding potential regulatory penalties.\n\nThe agreement reached with the nine companies also encompasses $150 billion in combined new investment commitments in domestic manufacturing, research and development of pharmaceuticals.\n\nThe agreements reduce prices on drugs that treat numerous costly and chronic conditions, including type two diabetes, rheumatoid arthritis, multiple sclerosis, asthma, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), hepatitis B and C, human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), and certain cancers.\n\n### Notable Donations\n\nBristol Myers Squibb announced that it will be giving for free to the Medicaid program its signature blood thinner Eliquis, prescribed to reduce the risk of blood clots and stroke, which is the company's top prescribed drug as well as one of Medicaid's most widely-used medicines.\n\n### Criticisms and Limitations\n\nThe deals mainly impact Medicaid and cash purchases, leaving private insurance and Medicare prices largely unchanged.\n\nAll 16 drug companies that inked deals with the Trump administration still raised some of their prices for 2026. Drug companies, including the 16 that made deals, raised the prices of 872 brand-name drugs in the first two weeks of 2026, according to an analysis by 46brooklyn.\n\nThe price increases came in at a median of 4% — the same as last year — despite the deals announced with fanfare by the Trump administration.\n\nA health policy researcher noted that \"Those deals probably are not very important in terms of manufacturer drug pricing and the prices paid by most Americans for prescription drugs.\"\n\nMany of the largest drugmakers may be exempt from Medicare pilot programs intended to force them to lower some of their prices. Several of the 14 pharmaceutical companies that struck individual drug-pricing deals with the White House said they are exempt from the Medicare effort.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"a109681f-e2a9-4882-817e-265be392e3e0","tool_use_result":{"query":"pharmaceutical companies Medicaid drug pricing deals Trump 2025 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01GMpnj1ooUxRy7RKR7nLcmx","content":[{"title":"WATCH: Trump announces 9 pharmaceutical companies will lower drug prices | PBS News","url":"https://www.pbs.org/newshour/health/watch-live-trump-expected-to-make-announcement-about-lowering-drug-prices"},{"title":"Trump Announces Pricing Deals With 9 Drugmakers, Expanding Most-Favored-Nation Drug Pricing Strategy | Pharmacy Times","url":"https://www.pharmacytimes.com/view/trump-announces-pricing-deals-with-9-drugmakers-expanding-most-favored-nation-drug-pricing-strategy"},{"title":"Trump announces new drugmaker deals to lower drug costs, boost US investment | Fox Business","url":"https://www.foxbusiness.com/politics/trump-secures-agreements-major-drugmakers-lower-medicaid-prescription-costs-americans"},{"title":"Fact Sheet: President Donald J. Trump Announces Largest Developments to Date in Bringing Most-Favored-Nation Pricing to American Patients – The White House","url":"https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2025/12/fact-sheet-president-donald-j-trump-announces-largest-developments-to-date-in-bringing-most-favored-nation-pricing-to-american-patients/"},{"title":"Trump struck deals with 16 drug companies. But they're still raising prices this year","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/01/16/nx-s1-5678915/trumprx-pharma-drug-price-deals-list-prices"},{"title":"Pharma Companies Raise List Prices, Including 16 That Had Agreements to Lower Prices with Trump Administration: Report | PharmExec","url":"https://www.pharmexec.com/view/companies-raise-list-prices-16-agreements-lower-prices-trump-administration-report"},{"title":"Drug Pricing in the Era of Trump 2.0 | Medicare Policy Initiative","url":"https://medicare.chir.georgetown.edu/drug-pricing-in-the-era-of-trump-2-0/"},{"title":"J&J Agreement Brings 15 of 17 Pharma Companies Into Trump's Drug-Pricing Effort | AJMC","url":"https://www.ajmc.com/view/j-j-agreement-brings-15-of-17-pharma-companies-into-trump-s-drug-pricing-effort"},{"title":"Nine drugmakers cut deal with Trump administration to slash medication costs","url":"https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/nine-drugmakers-cut-deal-trump-administration-slash-medication-costs-rcna250138"},{"title":"Pharma companies with Trump deals may avoid Medicare price cuts | STAT","url":"https://www.statnews.com/2025/12/23/trump-drug-pricing-deals-medicare-most-favored-nation-demos/"}]},"Based on my search results, here's what I found about pharmaceutical companies, Medicaid drug pricing deals, and the Trump administration in 2025-2026:\n\n## Overview of the Drug Pricing Deals\n\nPresident Trump announced agreements with major pharmaceutical companies to lower prescription drug prices for Americans in line with the lowest prices paid by other developed nations (known as the most-favored-nation, or MFN, price).\n\n### Companies Involved\n\nPharmaceutical companies Amgen, Bristol Myers Squibb, Boehringer Ingelheim, Genentech, Gilead Sciences, GSK, Merck, Novartis and Sanofi agreed to rein in Medicaid drug prices to match what they charged in other developed countries.\n\nOther major drugmakers including Pfizer, AstraZeneca, EMD Serono, Novo Nordisk and Eli Lilly struck similar deals with the Trump administration earlier in 2025.\n\nWith Johnson & Johnson's participation, 15 of 17 companies contacted by the administration over the summer have now signed on.\n\n### Key Details of the Deals\n\nThe agreements include direct-to-consumer sales, bypassing insurance, with a federal platform, TrumpRx.gov, launching in 2026. Companies aligning with Most Favored Nation pricing receive a 3-year tariff suspension, avoiding potential regulatory penalties.\n\nThe agreement reached with the nine companies also encompasses $150 billion in combined new investment commitments in domestic manufacturing, research and development of pharmaceuticals.\n\nThe agreements reduce prices on drugs that treat numerous costly and chronic conditions, including type two diabetes, rheumatoid arthritis, multiple sclerosis, asthma, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), hepatitis B and C, human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), and certain cancers.\n\n### Notable Donations\n\nBristol Myers Squibb announced that it will be giving for free to the Medicaid program its signature blood thinner Eliquis, prescribed to reduce the risk of blood clots and stroke, which is the company's top prescribed drug as well as one of Medicaid's most widely-used medicines.\n\n### Criticisms and Limitations\n\nThe deals mainly impact Medicaid and cash purchases, leaving private insurance and Medicare prices largely unchanged.\n\nAll 16 drug companies that inked deals with the Trump administration still raised some of their prices for 2026. Drug companies, including the 16 that made deals, raised the prices of 872 brand-name drugs in the first two weeks of 2026, according to an analysis by 46brooklyn.\n\nThe price increases came in at a median of 4% — the same as last year — despite the deals announced with fanfare by the Trump administration.\n\nA health policy researcher noted that \"Those deals probably are not very important in terms of manufacturer drug pricing and the prices paid by most Americans for prescription drugs.\"\n\nMany of the largest drugmakers may be exempt from Medicare pilot programs intended to force them to lower some of their prices. Several of the 14 pharmaceutical companies that struck individual drug-pricing deals with the White House said they are exempt from the Medicare effort."],"durationSeconds":22.030724400000004}}
[2026-02-04T17:13:25.122Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q4dZdkc26W7Y9eLVbdQoNm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"TrumpRx pharma drug price deals January 2026 list prices 872 drugs\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Trump struck deals with 16 drug companies. But they're still raising prices this year\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2026/01/16/nx-s1-5678915/trumprx-pharma-drug-price-deals-list-prices\"},{\"title\":\"Pharma Companies Raise List Prices, Including 16 That Had Agreements to Lower Prices with Trump Administration: Report | PharmExec\",\"url\":\"https://www.pharmexec.com/view/companies-raise-list-prices-16-agreements-lower-prices-trump-administration-report\"},{\"title\":\"TrumpRx\",\"url\":\"https://trumprx.gov/\"},{\"title\":\"FinancialContent - The Pharma Reckoning: 2026 Earnings Unveil a New Era of 'TrumpRx' Deals and Looming Patent Cliffs\",\"url\":\"https://markets.financialcontent.com/stocks/article/marketminute-2026-2-2-the-pharma-reckoning-2026-earnings-unveil-a-new-era-of-trumprx-deals-and-looming-patent-cliffs\"},{\"title\":\"WATCH: Trump announces 9 pharmaceutical companies will lower drug prices | PBS News\",\"url\":\"https://www.pbs.org/newshour/health/watch-live-trump-expected-to-make-announcement-about-lowering-drug-prices\"},{\"title\":\"Trump secures deals with nine pharma firms to lower US drug prices, avert tariffs | Invezz\",\"url\":\"https://invezz.com/news/2025/12/19/trump-secures-deals-with-nine-pharma-firms-to-lower-us-drug-prices-avert-tariffs/\"},{\"title\":\"Art of the drug deal: TrumpRX website will direct patients to heavily discounted medicines - Washington Times\",\"url\":\"https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2026/jan/9/art-drug-deal-trumprx-website-direct-patients-heavily-discounted/\"},{\"title\":\"TrumpRx and GLP-1s: What this means for drug pricing and employer strategies\",\"url\":\"https://www.wtwco.com/en-us/insights/2025/12/trumprx-and-glp-1s-what-this-means-for-drug-pricing-and-employer-strategies\"},{\"title\":\"Drug Pricing in the Era of Trump 2.0 | Medicare Policy Initiative\",\"url\":\"https://medicare.chir.georgetown.edu/drug-pricing-in-the-era-of-trump-2-0/\"},{\"title\":\"Federal Update: Trump Administration Announces Deal to Bring Most-Favored-Nation Pricing to GLP-1s | AMCP.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.amcp.org/letters-statements-analysis/federal-update-trump-administration-announces-deal-bring-most-favored-nation-pricing-glp-1s\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the TrumpRx pharma drug price deals and list prices in January 2026:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### Price Increases Despite Deals\nDrug companies, including the 16 that made deals with the Trump administration, raised the prices of 872 brand-name drugs in the first two weeks of 2026, according to a new analysis by 46brooklyn, a drug price research firm.\n\nThe price increases came in at a median of 4% — the same as last year — despite the deals announced with fanfare by the Trump administration.\n\n### Companies Involved\nAll 16 drug companies that inked deals with the Trump administration over the past few months still raised some of their prices for 2026. Since September, 16 major drug companies have inked deals with the Trump administration to lower prices.\n\nPharmaceutical companies Amgen, Bristol Myers Squibb, Boehringer Ingelheim, Genentech, Gilead Sciences, GSK, Merck, Novartis and Sanofi agreed to rein in Medicaid drug prices to match what they charged in other developed countries.\n\n### Specific Examples\nPfizer, which reached the first deal with the Trump administration in September, raised the prices of 72 products in January, according to 46brooklyn. They include a 15% increase on the price of its COVID shot.\n\nAdditionally, Merck raised prices for 18 medications, including Isentress for HIV and Belsomra for insomnia, according to data from 46Brooklyn.\n\n### TrumpRx Platform\nThe January 1, 2026, launch of TrumpRx.gov culminated as a federal site offering discounted cash-pay prices for chronic medications.\n\nThe deals included pledges for future drugs to be launched at the same price in other wealthy countries as in the U.S. And some drugs will be made available at a discount to cash-paying customers — that is, those who are uninsured or not using their health insurance — through a new website called TrumpRx.gov.\n\n### Expert Analysis\nAntonio Ciaccia, CEO of 46brooklyn, stated: \"The real truth serum is what's happening in the marketplace after those deals occur. January is prime time for list price changes on brand-name drugs. So in examining where we are today, we're pretty much in line with the last few years.\"\n\nThe deals don't affect prices for a lot of the companies' products and most health care consumers and insurance plans. According to health policy researcher Rome, \"Those deals probably are not very important in terms of manufacturer drug pricing and the prices paid by most Americans for prescription drugs.\"\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"286b1281-96a0-48df-a49b-d73adb3e1292","tool_use_result":{"query":"TrumpRx pharma drug price deals January 2026 list prices 872 drugs","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01AKxPnX4dehHpwNPgzoBawd","content":[{"title":"Trump struck deals with 16 drug companies. But they're still raising prices this year","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/01/16/nx-s1-5678915/trumprx-pharma-drug-price-deals-list-prices"},{"title":"Pharma Companies Raise List Prices, Including 16 That Had Agreements to Lower Prices with Trump Administration: Report | PharmExec","url":"https://www.pharmexec.com/view/companies-raise-list-prices-16-agreements-lower-prices-trump-administration-report"},{"title":"TrumpRx","url":"https://trumprx.gov/"},{"title":"FinancialContent - The Pharm