e are the search results on pharmaceutical lobbying, the Trump administration, campaign donations, and PhRMA in 2025-2026:\n\n## Lobbying Spending\n\nThe pharmaceutical industry spent $227 million on federal lobbying in the first half of 2025, on pace to easily surpass its all-time high of $388 million for 2024. The industry's main trade association, Pharmaceutical Research and Manufacturers of America (PhRMA), is consistently among the top spenders in Washington. In the first quarter of 2025 alone, PhRMA logged its highest-ever quarterly spending at nearly $13 million.\n\nPhRMA spent over $20.6 million on lobbying the federal government in the first half of 2025, including more than $7.6 million in the second quarter.\n\n## Inaugural Donations and Campaign Contributions\n\nPhRMA donated $1 million to Trump's 2025 inaugural fund but did not give to his campaign, according to OpenSecrets. FEC data suggests the group didn't donate to Trump or his Save America PAC in the 2024 election. It did, however, donate to a mix of Democratic and Republican House and Senate candidates.\n\nPhRMA, Pfizer, Bayer, Merck, Eli Lilly, and Abbott Labs each funneled between $500,000 and $1 million to Trump's 2025 inaugural committee.\n\nThe powerful drug lobby PhRMA donated $1 million to Trump's inauguration. So did drugmakers Bayer and Johnson & Johnson. The National Association of Manufacturers, a lobbying group that represents numerous industries, including the pharmaceutical sector, also donated $1 million.\n\n## Dark Money Donations\n\nRecords obtained by political watchdog group Issue One show that PhRMA last year gave millions to a Republican-aligned dark money group. PhRMA shelled out more than $5.6 million in political donations last year, including a $4 million donation to the American Action Network, a dark-money group aligned with House Republican leadership. Between 2020 and 2023, PhRMA funneled $17.5 million to the dark-money group.\n\nPhRMA donated $530,000 to groups involved with the far-right Project 2025 agenda.\n\n## Policy Wins and Lobbying Impact\n\nWeakening drug pricing rules helped turn PhRMA's $4 million dark-money contribution into an $8 billion windfall for drugmakers, according to a Congressional Budget Office estimate. At the behest of the pharmaceutical lobby — and after millions in political donations — Republican lawmakers have defanged rules that would lower the prices of life-saving medicines.\n\nEven as Trump administration threats loomed, the industry scored a major win this year with expanded orphan drug exemptions from Medicare price negotiations, showing that its influence in the Republican-controlled government remains formidable.\n\n## Industry Response to Trump Policies\n\nPhRMA, which donated $1 million to President Donald Trump's inaugural fund, came out against his new executive order aimed at lowering drug prices. When Trump reintroduced in May his \"most favored nation\" policy that seeks to peg US drug prices to cheaper ones paid abroad, PhRMA launched a campaign highlighting why Americans pay more for prescription medicine. Trump \"is right to use trade negotiations to force foreign governments to pay their fair share for medicines,\" but US patients \"should not foot the bill for global innovation.\""],"durationSeconds":22.441487600000002}}
[2026-02-04T17:13:54.122Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0143DwZR8QgDy4Be1FSU3ksF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"drug price increases 2024 2025 comparison year over year brand name medications\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Drug Channels: U.S. Brand-Name Drug Prices Fell in 2025 as the Net Pricing Drug Channel Emerges\",\"url\":\"https://www.drugchannels.net/2026/01/us-brand-name-drug-prices-fell-in-2025.html\"},{\"title\":\"Drug pricing 2024 year in review — 46brooklyn Research\",\"url\":\"https://www.46brooklyn.com/news/drug-pricing-2024-year-in-review-afn74h\"},{\"title\":\"Drug Channels: Inflation-Adjusted U.S. Brand-Name Drug Prices Fell for the Seventh Consecutive Year as a New Era of Drug Pricing Dawns\",\"url\":\"https://www.drugchannels.net/2025/01/inflation-adjusted-us-brand-name-drug.html\"},{\"title\":\"Pfizer, BMS and more ring in 2025 with fresh round of drug price increases: report\",\"url\":\"https://www.fiercepharma.com/pharma/pfizer-bms-and-more-ring-2025-fresh-round-drug-price-increases-report\"},{\"title\":\"CSRxP: BIG PHARMA RINGS IN 2026 WITH MORE THAN 300 PRICE INCREASES ON BRAND NAME DRUGS, OUTPACING START OF 2025 - CSRxP\",\"url\":\"https://www.csrxp.org/csrxp-big-pharma-rings-in-2026-with-more-than-300-price-increases-on-brand-name-drugs-outpacing-start-of-2025/\"},{\"title\":\"DOSE OF REALITY: BIG PHARMA’S PRICES FOR COSTLIEST 2025 MEDICATIONS OUTPACE FAIR PRICE ESTIMATES BASED ON CLINICAL VALUE - CSRxP\",\"url\":\"https://www.csrxp.org/dose-of-reality-big-pharmas-prices-for-costliest-2025-medications-outpace-fair-price-estimates-based-on-clinical-value/\"},{\"title\":\"National trends in prescription drug expenditures and projections for 2025 - PubMed\",\"url\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40263109/\"},{\"title\":\"Drug Channels: Inflation-Adjusted U.S. Brand-Name Drug Prices Fell for the Seventh Consecutive Year as a New Era of Drug Pricing Dawns (rerun)\",\"url\":\"https://www.drugchannels.net/2025/04/inflation-adjusted-us-brand-name-drug.html\"},{\"title\":\"U.S Insights: January 2024 Drug Price Changes\",\"url\":\"https://www.ipdanalytics.com/sample-reports-1/u.s-insights:-january-2024-drug-price-changes\"},{\"title\":\"Pharma to raise prices on more than 250 drugs in the US from January 2025 - Pharmaceutical Technology\",\"url\":\"https://www.pharmaceutical-technology.com/analyst-comment/pharma-prices-more-than-250-drugs-us-january-2025/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's a comprehensive comparison of drug price increases between 2024 and 2025 for brand-name medications:\n\n## Year-Over-Year Comparison: 2024 vs. 2025\n\n### List Price Trends\n\nFor 2024, average brand-name drugs' list prices grew by only 2.3%. For 2025, brand-name drugs' average list prices grew by only 3.5%, but net prices declined.\n\nThe amount of medicines seeing their price tags tick up in 2025 marks a sizable increase over the 140 branded drugs that underwent price hikes at the start of 2024. However, while the number of drugs becoming more costly is going up, the median scale of drug price increases has fallen significantly over the past decade, from 9% in 2015 to 4.5% in 2024.\n\n### January 2024 Price Changes\n\nBetween January 1, 2024, and January 31, 2024, more than 700 brand drugs had price increases of an average of 5.4% (median, 5%), and approximately 40 generic drug prices increased by an average of 39% (median, 10%), based on wholesale acquisition cost (WAC).\n\n### January 2025 Price Changes\n\nThe data reports that nearly all drug price increases are below 10% and the median price increase of the drugs in January 2025 is 4.5%. This shows a similar trend with an average price increase of 4.0% in January 2025 compared to December 2024 across 445 branded medicines that underwent a price change.\n\n### Historical Context\n\nFrom 2010 to 2015, growth in list prices had been increasing by 10% to 15%. Growth has slowed sharply. From 2019 through 2023, average list price increases had been about 5%.\n\n### Net Prices (After Rebates and Discounts)\n\nNet prices for brand-name drug prices were essentially unchanged. Through the first three quarters of 2024, nominal net prices increased by 0.1%. The gross-to-net gap in prices was therefore a historically small −2.2%.\n\nWhen manufacturers' rebates and discounts are factored in, drugs' average net prices—both before and after inflation—fell. After adjusting for overall inflation, brand-name drug net prices dropped for an unprecedented seventh consecutive year.\n\n### Notable Price Decreases\n\nMost notably, the three major manufacturers of widely prescribed insulin products—Eli Lilly, Novo Nordisk, and Sanofi—all reduced the WAC list price of many brand-name insulin products by −50% to −80%. These products had more than $20 billion in gross sales prior to the price reductions.\n\nFor 2024 and 2025, manufacturers reduced the wholesale acquisition cost (WAC) list prices for more than 20 brand-name drugs. For 2026, manufacturers will cut prices on at least 15 more drugs, which will reduce gross brand-name revenues by $35 to $40 billion. List prices are dropping by –25% to –85%.\n\n### Specific 2025 Price Increases\n\nPfizer's Paxlovid is set to receive a 3% price increase in 2025, while migraine treatment Nurtec and cancer drugs Adcetris, Ibrance and Xeljanz will see their list prices go up between 3% and 5%.\n\nAs for the biggest price increases of the new year, the 2025 prize goes to Leadiant Pharmaceuticals, which is hiking the price of its Hodgkin's disease drug Matulane by around 15% and slapping a 20% price increase on its Cystaran eye drops.\n\n### Overall Drug Spending Projections\n\nFor 2025, overall prescription drug spending is expected to rise by 9.0 to 11.0%, whereas in clinics and hospitals an 11.0% to 13.0% increase and a 2.0% to 4.0% increase, respectively, is anticipated compared to 2024.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"90b0bf73-7459-4818-a99e-400a3e98c630","tool_use_result":{"query":"drug price increases 2024 2025 comparison year over year brand name medications","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018PxrnRm8LsLN5AvFCLgcQ1","content":[{"title":"Drug Channels: U.S. Brand-Name Drug Prices Fell in 2025 as the Net Pricing Drug Channel Emerges","url":"https://www.drugchannels.net/2026/01/us-brand-name-drug-prices-fell-in-2025.html"},{"title":"Drug pricing 2024 year in review — 46brooklyn Research","url":"https://www.46brooklyn.com/news/drug-pricing-2024-year-in-review-afn74h"},{"title":"Drug Channels: Inflation-Adjusted U.S. Brand-Name Drug Prices Fell for the Seventh Consecutive Year as a New Era of Drug Pricing Dawns","url":"https://www.drugchannels.net/2025/01/inflation-adjusted-us-brand-name-drug.html"},{"title":"Pfizer, BMS and more ring in 2025 with fresh round of drug price increases: report","url":"https://www.fiercepharma.com/pharma/pfizer-bms-and-more-ring-2025-fresh-round-drug-price-increases-report"},{"title":"CSRxP: BIG PHARMA RINGS IN 2026 WITH MORE THAN 300 PRICE INCREASES ON BRAND NAME DRUGS, OUTPACING START OF 2025 - CSRxP","url":"https://www.csrxp.org/csrxp-big-pharma-rings-in-2026-with-more-than-300-price-increases-on-brand-name-drugs-outpacing-start-of-2025/"},{"title":"DOSE OF REALITY: BIG PHARMA’S PRICES FOR COSTLIEST 2025 MEDICATIONS OUTPACE FAIR PRICE ESTIMATES BASED ON CLINICAL VALUE - CSRxP","url":"https://www.csrxp.org/dose-of-reality-big-pharmas-prices-for-costliest-2025-medications-outpace-fair-price-estimates-based-on-clinical-value/"},{"title":"National trends in prescription drug expenditures and projections for 2025 - PubMed","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40263109/"},{"title":"Drug Channels: Inflation-Adjusted U.S. Brand-Name Drug Prices Fell for the Seventh Consecutive Year as a New Era of Drug Pricing Dawns (rerun)","url":"https://www.drugchannels.net/2025/04/inflation-adjusted-us-brand-name-drug.html"},{"title":"U.S Insights: January 2024 Drug Price Changes","url":"https://www.ipdanalytics.com/sample-reports-1/u.s-insights:-january-2024-drug-price-changes"},{"title":"Pharma to raise prices on more than 250 drugs in the US from January 2025 - Pharmaceutical Technology","url":"https://www.pharmaceutical-technology.com/analyst-comment/pharma-prices-more-than-250-drugs-us-january-2025/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's a comprehensive comparison of drug price increases between 2024 and 2025 for brand-name medications:\n\n## Year-Over-Year Comparison: 2024 vs. 2025\n\n### List Price Trends\n\nFor 2024, average brand-name drugs' list prices grew by only 2.3%. For 2025, brand-name drugs' average list prices grew by only 3.5%, but net prices declined.\n\nThe amount of medicines seeing their price tags tick up in 2025 marks a sizable increase over the 140 branded drugs that underwent price hikes at the start of 2024. However, while the number of drugs becoming more costly is going up, the median scale of drug price increases has fallen significantly over the past decade, from 9% in 2015 to 4.5% in 2024.\n\n### January 2024 Price Changes\n\nBetween January 1, 2024, and January 31, 2024, more than 700 brand drugs had price increases of an average of 5.4% (median, 5%), and approximately 40 generic drug prices increased by an average of 39% (median, 10%), based on wholesale acquisition cost (WAC).\n\n### January 2025 Price Changes\n\nThe data reports that nearly all drug price increases are below 10% and the median price increase of the drugs in January 2025 is 4.5%. This shows a similar trend with an average price increase of 4.0% in January 2025 compared to December 2024 across 445 branded medicines that underwent a price change.\n\n### Historical Context\n\nFrom 2010 to 2015, growth in list prices had been increasing by 10% to 15%. Growth has slowed sharply. From 2019 through 2023, average list price increases had been about 5%.\n\n### Net Prices (After Rebates and Discounts)\n\nNet prices for brand-name drug prices were essentially unchanged. Through the first three quarters of 2024, nominal net prices increased by 0.1%. The gross-to-net gap in prices was therefore a historically small −2.2%.\n\nWhen manufacturers' rebates and discounts are factored in, drugs' average net prices—both before and after inflation—fell. After adjusting for overall inflation, brand-name drug net prices dropped for an unprecedented seventh consecutive year.\n\n### Notable Price Decreases\n\nMost notably, the three major manufacturers of widely prescribed insulin products—Eli Lilly, Novo Nordisk, and Sanofi—all reduced the WAC list price of many brand-name insulin products by −50% to −80%. These products had more than $20 billion in gross sales prior to the price reductions.\n\nFor 2024 and 2025, manufacturers reduced the wholesale acquisition cost (WAC) list prices for more than 20 brand-name drugs. For 2026, manufacturers will cut prices on at least 15 more drugs, which will reduce gross brand-name revenues by $35 to $40 billion. List prices are dropping by –25% to –85%.\n\n### Specific 2025 Price Increases\n\nPfizer's Paxlovid is set to receive a 3% price increase in 2025, while migraine treatment Nurtec and cancer drugs Adcetris, Ibrance and Xeljanz will see their list prices go up between 3% and 5%.\n\nAs for the biggest price increases of the new year, the 2025 prize goes to Leadiant Pharmaceuticals, which is hiking the price of its Hodgkin's disease drug Matulane by around 15% and slapping a 20% price increase on its Cystaran eye drops.\n\n### Overall Drug Spending Projections\n\nFor 2025, overall prescription drug spending is expected to rise by 9.0 to 11.0%, whereas in clinics and hospitals an 11.0% to 13.0% increase and a 2.0% to 4.0% increase, respectively, is anticipated compared to 2024."],"durationSeconds":23.338357899999995}}
[2026-02-04T17:13:55.725Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018KFaRTo9mwgW8X5Demkz9c","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Trump pharma deals tariff exemption exchange drug pricing voluntary agreements 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Trump Strikes 9 New Pricing Agreements as Drugmakers Navigate Tariff, Regulatory Pressure | AJMC\",\"url\":\"https://www.ajmc.com/view/trump-strikes-9-new-pricing-agreements-as-drugmakers-navigate-tariff-regulatory-pressure\"},{\"title\":\"Nine of the largest pharma companies ink deals with Trump to lower drug prices\",\"url\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/19/nine-pharma-companies-ink-deals-with-trump-to-lower-drug-prices.html\"},{\"title\":\"J&J Agreement Brings 15 of 17 Pharma Companies Into Trump's Drug-Pricing Effort | AJMC\",\"url\":\"https://www.ajmc.com/view/j-j-agreement-brings-15-of-17-pharma-companies-into-trump-s-drug-pricing-effort\"},{\"title\":\"Fact Sheet: President Donald J. Trump Announces Largest Developments to Date in Bringing Most-Favored-Nation Pricing to American Patients – The White House\",\"url\":\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2025/12/fact-sheet-president-donald-j-trump-announces-largest-developments-to-date-in-bringing-most-favored-nation-pricing-to-american-patients/\"},{\"title\":\"Biopharma climbs higher as 9 drugmakers ink ‘pandering’ drug price deals with Trump | BioPharma Dive\",\"url\":\"https://www.biopharmadive.com/news/trump-most-favored-nation-drug-price-deals/808466/\"},{\"title\":\"A Pivotal Week for Pharmaceutical Policy: Trump Administration Advances Tariff and Drug Pricing Initiatives | Mintz\",\"url\":\"https://www.mintz.com/insights-center/viewpoints/2146/2025-10-07-pivotal-week-pharmaceutical-policy-trump-administration\"},{\"title\":\"Pharmaceutical Policy in Motion Continued: Trump Inks Nine New Drug Pricing Deals | Mintz\",\"url\":\"https://www.mintz.com/insights-center/viewpoints/2146/2025-12-23-pharmaceutical-policy-motion-continued-trump-inks-nine\"},{\"title\":\"Trump, Pfizer agree to lower U.S. drug prices, exempt company from pharma tariffs\",\"url\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/09/30/trump-pfizer-drug-price-agreement.html\"},{\"title\":\"Trump's pharmaceutical tariff threat loses bite after Pfizer deal reassures drugmakers\",\"url\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/10/01/trump-pharmaceutical-tariffs-pfizer-deal.html\"},{\"title\":\"9 pharma giants reach US drug price deals with Trump administration\",\"url\":\"https://www.fiercepharma.com/pharma/top-drugmakers-reach-us-drug-price-deal-trump-administration\"}]\n\nBased on my search, here's what I found about the Trump administration's pharmaceutical deals involving tariff exemptions in exchange for drug pricing voluntary agreements in 2025:\n\n## Overview\n\nPresident Donald Trump announced agreements with major pharmaceutical companies to lower prescription drug prices for Americans in line with the lowest prices paid by other developed nations, known as the most-favored-nation (MFN) price.\n\n## Key Companies Involved\n\nEarlier in 2025, Trump announced agreements with Eli Lilly, Novo Nordisk, Pfizer, AstraZeneca and EMD Serono to sell certain drugs directly to patients at a discount, in exchange for exemptions from his planned pharmaceutical tariffs and other benefits, such as fast-tracked reviews of new drugs.\n\nIn December 2025, nine additional manufacturers joined, including Amgen, Bristol Myers Squibb, Boehringer Ingelheim, Genentech, Gilead Sciences, GSK, Merck, Novartis, and Sanofi.\n\nJohnson & Johnson's agreement with the Trump Administration aims to improve drug access and reduce costs, exempting the company from potential tariffs. The agreement involves selling drugs to Medicaid at European market prices and creating online storefronts for direct consumer access.\n\n## Structure of the Deals\n\nThe tariff exemptions offered in exchange for participation echo the administration's earlier use of trade policy as leverage. Nine pharmaceutical companies agreed to align US drug prices with European levels, focusing on Medicaid and direct-to-consumer sales.\n\nIn exchange, the companies agreed to a three-year grace period during which their products won't face Trump's planned pharmaceutical-specific tariffs — as long as the drugmakers further invest in U.S. manufacturing.\n\nIn the deals, drugmakers also pledged that when they introduce new products into the US market, they will price them at levels aligned with what they intend to charge in Europe and other high-income countries.\n\n## The TrumpRx Platform\n\nThe agreements require the nine companies to offer medicines at a deep discount off the list price when selling directly to American patients through TrumpRx. Patients will be able to see massive price reductions on numerous products.\n\nFor example, Amgen will reduce the price of its cholesterol-lowering drug Repatha from $573 to $239 for patients purchasing directly through TrumpRx.\n\n## Additional Commitments\n\nAs part of the agreements, several companies are donating active pharmaceutical ingredients to the Strategic Active Pharmaceutical Ingredients Reserve (SAPIR). GSK will contribute 98.8kg of albuterol, Bristol Myers Squibb will contribute tablets representing 6.5 tons of apixaban, and Merck will contribute 3.5 tons of ertapenem.\n\nJohnson & Johnson is investing $55 billion in U.S. manufacturing and R&D, with major projects in North Carolina and Pennsylvania.\n\n## Analyst Perspectives\n\nAnalysts see little effect on the bottom lines of biopharma companies, as they stand to stave off tariff pressure and receive other benefits from the agreements.\n\nParticipating companies receive tariff exemptions, while the agreements do not address high prices under private insurance or Medicare. The deals represent a significant voluntary pricing effort, but their impact on patient savings and broader industry participation remains uncertain.\n\nSome experts noted that if enough manufacturers continue striking voluntary pricing agreements with the administration, the proposed MFN demonstration models, GLOBE and GUARD, might never be released because MFN pricing could be achieved without them.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"0b18b813-e828-463e-9283-efa1d068eb63","tool_use_result":{"query":"Trump pharma deals tariff exemption exchange drug pricing voluntary agreements 2025","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01EYSxWfvFzP5j14vQiwpxqG","content":[{"title":"Trump Strikes 9 New Pricing Agreements as Drugmakers Navigate Tariff, Regulatory Pressure | AJMC","url":"https://www.ajmc.com/view/trump-strikes-9-new-pricing-agreements-as-drugmakers-navigate-tariff-regulatory-pressure"},{"title":"Nine of the largest pharma companies ink deals with Trump to lower drug prices","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/19/nine-pharma-companies-ink-deals-with-trump-to-lower-drug-prices.html"},{"title":"J&J Agreement Brings 15 of 17 Pharma Companies Into Trump's Drug-Pricing Effort | AJMC","url":"https://www.ajmc.com/view/j-j-agreement-brings-15-of-17-pharma-companies-into-trump-s-drug-pricing-effort"},{"title":"Fact Sheet: President Donald J. Trump Announces Largest Developments to Date in Bringing Most-Favored-Nation Pricing to American Patients – The White House","url":"https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2025/12/fact-sheet-president-donald-j-trump-announces-largest-developments-to-date-in-bringing-most-favored-nation-pricing-to-american-patients/"},{"title":"Biopharma climbs higher as 9 drugmakers ink ‘pandering’ drug price deals with Trump | BioPharma Dive","url":"https://www.biopharmadive.com/news/trump-most-favored-nation-drug-price-deals/808466/"},{"title":"A Pivotal Week for Pharmaceutical Policy: Trump Administration Advances Tariff and Drug Pricing Initiatives | Mintz","url":"