[2026-02-04T17:18:40.884Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01R9aNjwYZ7HmaL6PHrQoyE9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Research Complete\n\n**Verification Summary:** The original claim is **substantially verified**.\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n1. **Claim Accuracy**: All 16 pharmaceutical companies with Trump administration deals did raise prices on 872 brand-name drugs in January 2026, with a median increase of 4%—identical to the prior year, demonstrating no impact from the deals.\n\n2. **Scope Limitation Confirmed**: The deals primarily cover Medicaid patients (who already receive statutory rebates) and cash-paying customers via TrumpRx.gov (~8% of market). Commercial insurance and Medicare pricing remain unaffected.\n\n3. **Specific Examples**:\n   - Pfizer raised prices on 72 products including a 15% increase on its COVID vaccine\n   - Merck raised prices on 18 products\n   - GSK raised prices on ~20 products by 2-8.9%\n\n4. **Deal Structure**: Companies received 3-year tariff exemptions in exchange for voluntary, unenforceable commitments with confidential terms\n\n5. **Financial Context**: The pharmaceutical industry spent $227M on lobbying in H1 2025 (record pace) and donated $7-8M to Trump's inaugural fund during deal negotiations\n\n**Sources**: [NPR](https://www.npr.org/2026/01/16/nx-s1-5678915/trumprx-pharma-drug-price-deals-list-prices), [46brooklyn Research](https://www.46brooklyn.com/branddrug-boxscore), [AJMC](https://www.ajmc.com/view/j-j-agreement-brings-15-of-17-pharma-companies-into-trump-s-drug-pricing-effort), [Georgetown Medicare Policy](https://medicare.chir.georgetown.edu/drug-pricing-in-the-era-of-trump-2-0/)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11616,"cache_read_input_tokens":50782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11616},"output_tokens":1,"service_tie